\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 When Maya moved into her college dorm, she expected her first few weeks to be stressful. She had to meet new people, find all of her classes, and learn how to live on her own. One afternoon, while organizing her closet, she noticed something strange.\
Behind a stack of old boxes was a small wooden box covered in dust. It had a silver lock on the front, but there was no key. Maya picked it up and noticed a single letter carved into the top: \'93E.\'94\
She took the box to her roommate, Jordan.\
\'93Do you think someone left it here?\'94 Jordan asked.\
\'93Maybe,\'94 Maya said. \'93But why would they lock it?\'94\
The two girls searched the room but could not find anything that explained where the box came from. Maya decided to ask their resident assistant if the previous student had left anything behind.\
The RA checked the room records and discovered that the room had belonged to a student named Elena three years earlier. Maya became even more curious.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 That night, Maya woke up to a strange sound. The wooden box was sitting in the middle of the room.\
She was sure she had left it inside her closet.\
Maya slowly walked toward it. Suddenly, the silver lock clicked open by itself.\
Inside was a photograph of Maya.\
She froze.\
The picture showed her standing in the exact same dorm room, wearing the same clothes she had worn that day. On the back of the photograph was a message:\

\f1\b \strokec2 \'93You found it earlier than I expected.\'94
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
Maya immediately woke Jordan. They searched the room again and found another photograph hidden under the bed. It showed Elena standing beside the box.\
But Elena wasn't alone.\
Standing next to her was Maya's mother.\
Maya stared at the photograph in disbelief. She had never seen it before, and her mother had never mentioned Elena.\
Then her phone buzzed.\
It was a text from her mom:\

\f1\b \strokec2 \'93Maya, whatever you do, don't open the box.\'94
